<title>JAPAN: Japan builders fall on cross-shareholding cuts.</title>
<headline>Japan builders fall on cross-shareholding cuts.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Construction  sector issues fell in Monday morning trade, battered by the dissolution of cross-shareholdings, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0142 GMT, Obayashi Corp was down 40 yen at 592, a new low for the calendar year. Shimizu Corp was also at a new low for the year after losing 47 yen to trade at 503.  </p>
<p>&quot;Unlike the banking sector, which is being soothed by Nippon Credit Bank Ltd, there is no good news for builders,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>&quot;The shares will probably continue to search for a floor to rest on.&quot;</p>
</text>
